<title>GERMANY: Viag expects stable 1997 earnings.</title>
<headline>Viag expects stable 1997 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>German diversified utility Viag AG said on Tuesday it expected a rise in group sales in full-year 1997 and that it expected earnings to remain stable or rise slightly in the period.</p>
<p>Viag's chemical unit SKW Trostberg and its aluminium unit VAW Aluminium AG performed particularly well in the first half of 1997, Viag said.</p>
<p>Viag's business in the first half of the year was as expected, matching the previous year, the group's management board chairman Georg Obermeier said in the text of a speech prepared for delivery at the group's annual shareholders meeting.  </p>
<p>Obermeier said that there were no major problem areas in the group, but there were weak points in certain subsidiaries.</p>
<p>These included its stake in U.S. computer group AmeriQuest, which Obermeier said would be restructured and sold off this year.</p>
<p>The group said that problems at its Gerresheimer Glas unit would have limited impact on the group's earnings.</p>
<p>--Clifford Coonan, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
